# Accepted security exceptions. See docs/security-decisions.md for rationale.
# Review date: 2027-01-07

# readOnlyRootFilesystem on PostgreSQL.
# The database writes its unix socket and scratch files outside the data
# volume. Achievable with additional emptyDir mounts but low value on a
# single-tenant stateful workload whose data volume is writable regardless.
KSV-0014

# KSV-01010 "ConfigMap stores sensitive contents in key(s) or value(s)".
# Added 2026-10-20, review 2027-04-20.
#
# Fires on harbourline-config for the key DB_PORT, whose value is 5432. The
# rule matches on KEY NAMES against a heuristic list; a port number is not a
# secret and there is nothing to fix.
#
# KNOWN COST OF THIS EXCEPTION: it is repository-wide, so a real credential
# placed in a ConfigMap would also go unflagged by this rule. That risk is
# carried by three other controls - Trivy's secret scanner matches on value
# PATTERNS rather than key names, Kyverno blocks on admission, and secrets
# are created imperatively and never committed (docs/cluster-state-not-in-git.md).
KSV-01010

# KSV-0125 "uses an image from an untrusted registry".
# Added 2026-11-14, review 2027-05-14.
#
# Fires on curlimages/curl:8.11.1 in k8s/labs/rbac/01-reporter-no-role.yaml.
#
# WHAT CHANGED: nothing in this repository. That file was written on
# 2026-10-31 and passed every build since. Trivy's bundled policy set updated
# and began enforcing a check that was not previously applied. SonarCloud said
# the same thing in the same run - "the quality profile assigned to this
# project has changed".
#
# A SCANNER'S RULE SET IS A DEPENDENCY, and this one is not pinned. A green
# build is a statement about the rules on the day it ran, not a property of
# the code. Worth knowing before promising anyone that main is always
# releasable.
#
# WHY ACCEPTED: the image is the curl project's own, pinned to an exact tag,
# and the manifest is a teaching lab applied by hand - no Application
# references it and it reaches no cluster through the pipeline.
#
# THE REAL FIX, not done: mirror third-party images into GHCR and reference
# them by digest. That removes the finding honestly rather than silencing it,
# and removes the dependency on Docker Hub being up and unchanged at deploy
# time. The same image is used by the smoke-test Job inside helm/, which the
# config scan does not see at all - skip-dirs: helm is its own open debt.
KSV-0125
